Description: A track with cues loads at the first of them, like a CDJ
 Mixxx's default "load at" mode is the intro start, which a rekordbox track
 does not have until Mixxx has analysed it, so every track loaded at 0:00,
 memory cues or not. The import already makes the first memory cue the main
 cue; CueControl now seeks a loaded track to the earliest of the main cue and
 its hot cues (saved loops do not count). A track with neither loads by the
 configured mode as before. Only the "Beginning" mode still means 0:00, which
 keeps the vinyl-control needle drop working.
 .
 trackAnalyzed() applies the same rule when analysis finishes on a deck that
 has not been moved since the load: a track with no cues gets a main cue at
 its first sound from the silence analyser and moves there, and a track that
 loaded at its first cue stays on it instead of following the intro start the
 analyser adds.
 .
 No existing test moves: the tests that load a track with cues on it use
 SeekOnLoadMode::MainCue with only a main cue, where the first cue is the
 main cue. New tests: CueControlTest.SeekOnLoadFirstCue and
 SeekOnLoadMainCueWithoutHotcues.
Author: Pioneered CI <pioneered-build@localhost>
Forwarded: no
---
